  "Comments": "Silicon tetrafluoride SiF4, the fluorine gas of the phosphoric acid reactor and concentrator. Ideal gas formation enthalpy -1614.94 kJ/mol and the Shomate heat capacity (298 to 1000 K) of the NIST WebBook (Chase 1998), Tc 259 K and Pc 37.15 bar (Booth and Swinehart 1935). The vapor pressure joins the sublimation curve of Pace and Mosser (1963, 163 to 187 K) to the critical point; SiF4 is always a gas at process conditions. In water it hydrolyses to fluorosilicic acid and silica, which the plant writes as a reaction. Vapor pressure eq 101 within 3.4 % of the Pace-Mosser curve and the critical point. Acentric factor 0.385 and liquid density 1660 kg/m3 near the triple point (to be checked).",
